From: VIKING <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: enable IPQ9574 Direct Switch

IPQ9574 uses the same EDMA v2 shared-ring and buffer protocol as IPQ5332
in QSDK R48. Its CPU RXDESC20-23, RXFILL4-7 and TXDESC/TXCMPL8-31 leave
the native DS rings 1/2 free. Queues 32-47 stay separate from CPU RSS
queues 0-31, and the SoC DT already describes their six interrupts.

Allow the existing native provider on the IPQ9574 PPE compatible so
QCN9274 hw1.0/hw2.0 clients can register automatically. Keep identity
DMA, 32-bit shared-ring addressing, peer authorization, ordinary MLO/AHB
fallback and confirmed DMA shutdown requirements unchanged. No board
specific routing or replacement EDMA/NSS driver is needed.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-dp/-/tree/win_qsdk.common.1.0.r48
Signed-off-by: VIKING <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_ds.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_ds.c
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /* Native PPE Direct Switch ring transport.
  *
- * The IPQ5332 resource layout and ring aliasing follow the Qualcomm QSDK
+ * The EDMA v2 resource layout and ring aliasing follow the Qualcomm QSDK
  * nss-dp EDMA v2 PPE-DS implementation. PPE RXDESC aliases WLAN PPE2TCL;
  * PPE TXDESC aliases WLAN REO2PPE. CPU work is limited to index handoff,
  * batched buffer refill and completion, never per-packet skb transmission.
@@ -991,7 +991,8 @@
 	char name[24];
 	int node, i, ret = 0;
 
-	if (!of_device_is_compatible(ppe_dev->dev->of_node, "qcom,ipq5332-ppe"))
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(ppe_dev->dev->of_node, "qcom,ipq5332-ppe") &&
+	    !of_device_is_compatible(ppe_dev->dev->of_node, "qcom,ipq9574-ppe"))
 		return 0;
 	provider = kzalloc(sizeof(*provider), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!provider)
